    "chunk_text": "Autodoc 360 relocates to reinforce commitment to premium auto care\n\nAutodoc 360 (Pvt) Ltd, a leading name in premium automotive service and repair, has officially shifted operations to No. 378/2/C, Koswatta Road, Kalapaluwawa, Rajagiriya, a new, larger, and more advanced facility, marking a significant milestone in the company\u2019s growth journey in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe relocation reflects Autodoc 360\u2019s steady expansion and rising demand among owners of luxury and performance vehicles. The new premises have been purpose-designed to accommodate advanced diagnostic bays, precision repair zones, and a significantly enhanced parts inventory\u2014ensuring faster turnaround times and superior service quality for customers.\n\nAccording to the management, relocation was driven by the need to support high-end European vehicles, especially BMW and Mercedes-Benz, which require specialised infrastructure, tooling, and technical expertise. The new workshop allows the team to operate with manufacturer-grade accuracy while maintaining international workshop standards.\n\nA key strength of Autodoc 360 lies in its technical backbone. The workshop is staffed by technicians from authorised dealership backgrounds, each with 10 to 15+ years of hands-on experience with luxury vehicles. The facility is equipped with German OEM-grade tools and diagnostic systems that meet European workshop standards, ensuring precise fault detection and manufacturer-accurate repairs rather than generic trial-and-error solutions. On the customer-facing side, Head Service Advisor Ranil Alwis brings several years of experience at authorised BMW workshops and deep expertise in German and European automotive technology, particularly BMW and Mercedes-Benz standards. His ability to accurately assess issues, coordinate manufacturer-aligned repair processes, and communicate technical matters clearly and reassuringly makes him an integral part of Autodoc 360\u2019s service delivery."
