    "chunk_text": "Among all festivals, the Spring Festival holds the highest place. Among all seasons, spring stands as the first. As the most ancient, grand and important traditional festival in China, the Spring Festival represents the cultural roots and emotional bonds of the Chinese people, embodies their devotion to family and country, and conveys the values of peace, goodwill and harmony. Although originating in China, the Spring Festival now belongs to the world. Having been inscribed on UNESCO\u2019s Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, its global influence continues to grow. The Spring Festival is increasingly becoming a window to showcase Chinese culture and a bridge for cultural exchange and mutual learning among civilisations.\n\nExtraordinary chapter on the journey toward building a great country\n\nOver the past year, our compatriots in Sri Lanka have worked hard in unity to realise shared dreams. The robust progress in China-Sri Lanka relations is inseparable from the dedicated efforts of our compatriots. Chinese companies have overcome difficulties and shouldered significant responsibilities, contributing to bilateral economic and trade cooperation. Chinese teachers and students have promoted Chinese culture and told China\u2019s stories well. Overseas Chinese have remained deeply connected to their roots, giving back to their homeland with sincerity and action. Everyone present here has played an important role in deepening exchanges and cooperation and enhancing the friendship between our two peoples. The Chinese Embassy in Sri Lanka has also actively implemented the vision of \u201cpeople-centred diplomacy\u201d, continuously improved the quality and efficiency of consular services, and made every effort to address the concerns of our compatriots. With dedication and compassion, we have worked to protect the legitimate rights and interests of Chinese institutions and citizens in Sri Lanka."
